        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: చెడగొట్టు",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చెడగొట్టు — ceḍagoṭṭu — \"to spoil; to ruin\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "వర్షం మా విహారయాత్రను చెడగొట్టింది. varṣaṁ mā vihārayātranu ceḍagoṭṭindi. The rain spoiled our outing."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): చెడగొట్టాను, ceḍagoṭṭānu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చెడ, bad, + కొట్టు, to strike: to make something go bad. Said of plans, food and children who are spoilt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "చెడగొట్టు (ceḍagoṭṭu) is native Dravidian: చెడు, \"to go bad\" (DEDR 2760), and కొట్టు, \"to strike\" (DEDR 2063)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
